From a6f32b11591e14de20bd68a617aa4e1ab4e956fd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gabriel Fernandez <gabriel.fernandez@foss.st.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Feb 2026 15:26:50 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 376/913] drivers: scmi-msg: initialize status for unused clock
 config type

Without this initialization, the function returns an error status,
leading to:

  scmi-clocks scmi_dev.2|4: Failed to get state for clock ID [2-30]

This makes the default/unused extended config path return a valid success
status and avoids spurious clock state query failures.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [ST downstream https://github.com/STMicroelectronics/optee_os.git b98dd91fbce0b4a89bcbf4bd051436a57a0ccd8c drivers: scmi-msg: initialize status for unused clock config type]
Signed-off-by: Gabriel Fernandez <gabriel.fernandez@foss.st.com>
Change-Id: Ib749095d7d9aaa535cb9c4c9c8121ba7add623bc
Reviewed-on: https://gerrit.st.com/c/mpu/oe/optee/optee_os/+/562468
Reviewed-by: Thomas BOURGOIN <thomas.bourgoin@foss.st.com>
ACI: CIBUILD <MDG-smet-aci-builds@list.st.com>
Domain-Review: Patrick DELAUNAY <patrick.delaunay@foss.st.com>
ACI: CITOOLS <MDG-smet-aci-reviews@list.st.com>
---
 core/drivers/scmi-msg/clock.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/core/drivers/scmi-msg/clock.c b/core/drivers/scmi-msg/clock.c
index 8ba6d4af2..50558292d 100644
--- a/core/drivers/scmi-msg/clock.c
+++ b/core/drivers/scmi-msg/clock.c
@@ -393,6 +393,7 @@ static void scmi_clock_config_get(struct scmi_msg *msg)
 
 	switch (in_args->flags & SCMI_CLOCK_CONFIG_GET_EXT_TYPE_MASK) {
 	case SCMI_CLOCK_EXTENDED_CONFIG_TYPE_UNUSED:
+		status = SCMI_SUCCESS;
 		break;
 	case SCMI_CLOCK_EXTENDED_CONFIG_TYPE_DUTY_CYCLE:
 		status = get_duty_cycle(msg->channel_id, clock_id,
-- 
